## The `Units.Natural` module of §8.20.
##
## §5.3.4 describes `Units.Natural` as "a system of units in which `c = 1` and
## `hbar = 1`", not as a set of constants with changed values. This build does
## not ship that system: a natural-unit table would be a *second* unit table
## beside the kernel manifest, which §5.4 rules out, and the kernel has no
## natural-unit registry to project. The module exists so `import Units.Natural`
## resolves (§8.20 requires the tree), and exports nothing.
##
## What works today: the physical constants are values, not units, so `c` and
## `hbar` belong to `Units.Constants` (generated from `manifest.constants`) and
## to `Rssn.Constants`; `GeV` is `eV` with the `G` prefix. A real natural-unit
## system needs a kernel registry (reported as a remaining gap).
module Units.Natural
